/-
# Obsmetrologia — the relational-generative mathematics library

A **dependency-free** Lean 4 library (no Mathlib; Lean core only) that is the
inductive derivation tree of `561-group/content/`. Each module is generated by the
one before it — read the import spine top-to-bottom and it is a proof.

The rule the whole library obeys: **past `Mark` and `Articulating` there is no free
data.** Those two modules admit the only primitives — the atomic marks and the
articulating recursion. Every module below them *derives* its content; none
introduces an `axiom`, `opaque`, or `constant`.

## The spine so far

* `Obsmetrologia.Mark`             — the arbitrary atomic primitive; two kinds by position.
* `Obsmetrologia.Utterance`        — the ordered pair (token, claim); articulating's domain.
* `Obsmetrologia.Articulating`     — the base morphism; recursive `[utterance, articulating]`.
* `Obsmetrologia.Articulating.Cell` — articulating's codomain; the derived four-cell partition.
* `Obsmetrologia.Predicating`      — the morphism out of the potential cell; the predication
                               category and its object φ = (s, p, o). Category theory.
* `Obsmetrologia.Positing`         — admits value: the FOUR bilattice of readings (= the four
                               phases met as value), the valuation, the ⊥ₖ seed.
* `Obsmetrologia.FregeanFourChu`   — independent evidence on an oriented predication is
                               FOUR's two slots, read through the predication Chu
                               space (a finite correspondence; the forcing is
                               `Orbital.orbital_exhaustive`).
* `Obsmetrologia.Settling`         — the closure ◇∘□ to its fixed point; **generates order**:
                               `≤ₖ` proven a partial order, `∨ₖ`/`∧ₖ` its lub/glb,
                               Knaster–Tarski least fixed point.
* `Obsmetrologia.Hyperdoctrine`    — quantifier adjoints over reindexing; the converse
                               adjoint system `∃ ⊣ f* ⊣ ∀`, Frobenius, Beck–Chevalley.
* `Obsmetrologia.Quantifying`      — the fiber quantifier adjoints `∃_f ⊣ f* ⊣ ∀_f` for any
                               finite fibration (covers the projection generators).
* `Obsmetrologia.TruthOrder`       — the bilattice's **second** order `≤ₜ` as a bounded
                               lattice + truth-order closure; negation is the duality.
* `Obsmetrologia.ClosureOrdinal`   — settling iterated to its fixed point; the closure
                               ordinal `κ ≤ 3` — the **strict-finite regime**.
* `Obsmetrologia.Sheaf`            — settling's fixed point as a sheaf `{base, section}`;
                               **H¹ = 0** (CRDT/CALM convergence) + sheaf separation.
* `Obsmetrologia.Four`             — the capstone: the recurring FOUR is one object (phases =
                               readings = generators); the **Klein-four symmetry** `⟨~,−⟩`.
* `Obsmetrologia.Positing.Bigraded`  — the first math structure *below* settling: two commuting
                               **nuclei** → the **nuclear quartet** (FOUR as sub-algebras).
* `Obsmetrologia.Equality`         — the **second adjoint system** `∃^t⊣f*⊣∀^t` (truth order);
                               classical & paraconsistent **equality derived**, not posited.
* `Obsmetrologia.Closure.Monad`     — the closure-2-monad's KZ/lax-idempotence reduction
                               (`kz_iff_strict`, no periodic orbits, `F_U=Cl∨ₖu` settles).
* `Obsmetrologia.BigradedCohomology` — a classification table of readings (consistent /
                               paraconsistent / mixed) + the internal **ℤ/2 gauge** (`~`).
* `Obsmetrologia.Settlement`       — the recurring site/settlement shape (a bare base paired
                               with content admitted by its own law), instantiated here at
                               the bitopological settling site's Čech gluing.
* `Obsmetrologia.AperiodicOrder`   — aperiodic tilings: the substitution-system/tiling core,
                               the port-graph and lenticle carriers, and their moduli.

## Pure mathematics only

This package holds mathematics and nothing else. Theory whose objects are physical, chemical,
material, craft, economic, or software entities lives in packages that import this one, in the
section that owns the subject:

* `ObsmetrologiaPhysicalScience` — causal sets, condensed matter (crystal, glass, defects),
  kinetic theory, thermodynamics, dense matter, quantum contextuality, reaction networks.
* `ObsmetrologiaMaterials` — material sectors, contact mechanics, vitrimer exchange.
* `ObsmetrologiaEconomics` — attention allocation, the allocation solver, currency cocones.
* `ObsmetrologiaFibercraft` — weave drafts and lenticle crossings.
* `ObsmetrologiaComputing` — program formats, Hoare programs, causality packets, game theory.

Nothing in this package may import any of them.
-/
